---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import status from "../../data/status.json";
const osStatus = status.entries.find((entry) => entry.id === "aurora-os-public-evidence");
const browserStatus = status.entries.find((entry) => entry.id === "lumen-browser-public-evidence");
---
<SiteLayout title="Aurora — Independent computing. Built deliberately." description="Discover Aurora OS and Lumen, the Aurora Browser. Independent computing, built deliberately and documented with evidence.">
  <section class="reference-hero">
    <div class="shell reference-hero-inner">
      <div class="reference-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> AN INDEPENDENT COMPUTING ECOSYSTEM</p>
        <h1>Build a better<br /><span>relationship with</span><br />your technology.</h1>
        <p class="reference-hero-description">Aurora is an independent project exploring a more deliberate approach to computing — from the foundations of an operating system to the tools people use every day.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#ecosystem">Explore the ecosystem <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reference-hero-art" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/aurora-hero.svg" alt="" width="760" height="480" fetchpriority="high" /></div>
      <div class="reference-hero-index"><span>01 / 02 <i></i></span><span>ONE ECOSYSTEM · MULTIPLE WORKSTREAMS</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="reference-principles" aria-label="Aurora principles"><div class="shell reference-principles-inner"><span>SECURITY BY DESIGN</span><b aria-hidden="true">✦</b><span>OPEN ENGINEERING</span><b aria-hidden="true">✦</b><span>MEASURED PROGRESS</span><b aria-hidden="true">✦</b><span>USER SOVEREIGNTY</span></div></section>
  <section class="home-intro shell" aria-labelledby="home-intro-title">
    <div class="home-intro-index"><span>01</span><span>THE IDEA</span></div>
    <div class="home-intro-main">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> COMPUTING, RECONSIDERED</p>
      <h2 id="home-intro-title">The tools we use<br />should make sense<br /><span>from the inside out.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="home-intro-aside">
      <p>Aurora is an independent computing project built around a simple belief: the systems we rely on should be understandable, secure by design and shaped around the people who use them.</p>
      <a class="home-inline-link" href="/en/engineering/">Explore our engineering approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-products" id="ecosystem" aria-labelledby="home-products-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="home-section-topline"><span>02 / THE ECOSYSTEM</span><span>TWO PRODUCTS · ONE DIRECTION</span></div>
      <div class="home-products-heading">
        <h2 id="home-products-title">A foundation.<br /><span>And what runs on it.</span></h2>
        <p>Aurora OS and Lumen are separate products with a shared direction. Each has its own engineering challenges, development path and evidence.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="home-product home-product-os">
        <div class="home-product-copy">
          <p class="home-product-kicker">01 — OPERATING SYSTEM</p>
          <h3>Aurora OS</h3>
          <p class="home-product-lead">A new foundation for personal computing.</p>
          <p>Built from scratch in Rust, Aurora OS follows a capability-based microkernel architecture. The project focuses on explicit authority, clear service boundaries and a system that can be understood and reasoned about.</p>
          <a class="home-inline-link" href="/en/ecosystem/os/">Discover Aurora OS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="home-os-progress" aria-label="Aurora OS project-reported development estimate">
          <div class="home-progress-label"><span>PROJECT-REPORTED PROGRESS</span><span>NOT A RELEASE READINESS SCORE</span></div>
          <div class="home-progress-number">{osStatus?.reportedProgress ?? 70}<span>%</span></div>
          <div class="home-progress-track" role="img" aria-label={`${osStatus?.reportedProgress ?? 70}% estimated progress reported by the project`}><span style={`--progress: ${osStatus?.reportedProgress ?? 70}%`}></span></div>
          <p>This percentage is the project's own development estimate. It is not an independently measured completion metric and does not imply that the OS is installable or production-ready.</p>
          <div class="home-os-tags"><span>RUST</span><span>MICROKERNEL</span><span>CAPABILITY-BASED</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="home-product home-product-lumen">
        <div class="home-lumen-art" aria-label="Lumen browser identity graphic">
          <div class="home-lumen-orbit home-lumen-orbit-one"></div>
          <div class="home-lumen-orbit home-lumen-orbit-two"></div>
          <div class="home-lumen-core"><span>L</span></div>
          <span class="home-lumen-art-label">LUMEN / 02</span>
          <span class="home-lumen-art-caption">BROWSER WORKSTREAM</span>
        </div>
        <div class="home-product-copy">
          <p class="home-product-kicker">02 — WEB BROWSER</p>
          <h3>Lumen</h3>
          <p class="home-product-lead">A considered way to explore the web.</p>
          <p>Lumen is the Aurora Browser, currently in development. It is a distinct application with its own architecture, compatibility requirements and security responsibilities. Its capabilities will be documented as they are implemented and verified.</p>
          <div class="home-lumen-status"><span class="home-status-pulse"></span>{browserStatus?.reportedStage?.toUpperCase() ?? "IN DEVELOPMENT"}</div>
          <a class="home-inline-link" href="/en/ecosystem/browser/">Discover Lumen <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-principles-editorial shell" aria-labelledby="home-principles-title">
    <div class="home-section-topline"><span>03 / WHAT GUIDES US</span><span>PRINCIPLES, NOT SLOGANS</span></div>
    <div class="home-principles-layout">
      <h2 id="home-principles-title">Good technology<br /><span>earns trust.</span></h2>
      <div class="home-principles-list">
        <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Security is structural.</h3><p>Privilege boundaries, isolation and failure containment belong in the architecture—not in a list of promises.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Privacy is deliberate.</h3><p>Collect less, explain data handling clearly and give people meaningful control.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Complexity should be legible.</h3><p>Prefer explicit interfaces, maintainable systems and decisions that can be inspected.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Progress needs evidence.</h3><p>Separate architectural intent, implementation, tests and release readiness. Never present one as another.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-explore" aria-labelledby="home-explore-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="home-section-topline"><span>04 / GO DEEPER</span><span>ENGINEERING · DOCUMENTATION · STATUS</span></div>
      <div class="home-explore-heading">
        <h2 id="home-explore-title">Look under<br /><span>the surface.</span></h2>
        <p>Follow the decisions, read the documentation and see what is actually being built.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="home-explore-links">
        <a href="/en/engineering/architecture/"><span class="home-explore-number">01</span><span class="home-explore-copy"><strong>Architecture</strong><small>System structure, responsibilities and interfaces</small></span><span class="home-explore-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/en/engineering/security/"><span class="home-explore-number">02</span><span class="home-explore-copy"><strong>Security</strong><small>Threats, privilege boundaries and limitations</small></span><span class="home-explore-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/en/docs/"><span class="home-explore-number">03</span><span class="home-explore-copy"><strong>Documentation</strong><small>Guides for users, developers and contributors</small></span><span class="home-explore-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/en/development/"><span class="home-explore-number">04</span><span class="home-explore-copy"><strong>Development status</strong><small>Reported progress, evidence and project roadmap</small></span><span class="home-explore-arrow">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-closing shell">
    <div class="home-closing-rule"></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> FOLLOW THE WORK</p><h2>Built in the open.<br /><span>Grounded in engineering.</span></h2><p>Explore the public repository, follow development and see how Aurora takes shape.</p></div>
    <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
